# Quran content configuration (optional — the app works without this file).
#
# Copy this file to `assets/env/quran_api.env` only when you need to point
# the app at your own hosts. The mushaf pages, translation/tafsir catalog and
# audio all fall back to public hosts + bundled data, so no configuration is
# required for a working build.
#
# WARNING: never commit the real .env file — it is git-ignored.
# You can also pass these at build time with --dart-define=KEY=value.
#
# ── Own mushaf page images (WebP) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The folder that directly contains `day/`, `night/`, `ayah_boxes.json` and
# `manifest.json`, e.g.:
#   QF_MUSHAF_BASE=https://cdn.example.com/quran/mushaf
#   QF_MUSHAF_BASE=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OWNER/REPO/main
# Empty falls back to the public GitHub repo.
QF_MUSHAF_BASE=

# ── Own content catalog (quran-content.json + tafsir/translation files) ────
# The folder that directly contains `quran-content.json`, e.g.:
#   QF_CONTENT_BASE=https://cdn.example.com/quran/content
#   QF_CONTENT_BASE=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OWNER/REPO/main
# Empty falls back to the public GitHub repo.
QF_CONTENT_BASE=
